id: pm-rl-81oc
title: "Generation lineage: a policy generation is an item whose parent is the generation that produced its training data"
description: "A Generation records the base checkpoint it started from, the policy that collected its training data, the Run ids of those collection episodes, and the training configuration that turned them into a successor. Its parent edge points at the generation whose policy did the collecting. Which generation produced this trajectory then stops being a question answered by a filename convention and becomes a reachability query over edges pm already stores and merges losslessly. The edge also carries the invalidation frontier for free: an environment edit reaches every descendant without pm-rl maintaining a second index of its own."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T20:49:37.421Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T20:49:37.421Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: A generation with no parent is accepted as the seed generation and reports itself as such; every later generation requires a parent that exists and is itself promoted; the collection runs named by a generation must reference the parent's policy and are refused when they do not; the recorded checkpoint identity is content-addressed so a silently swapped checkpoint fails to resolve
